      "name": "sync_fifo",
      "behavior": "Synchronous depth-16 FIFO of 8-bit words. Accepts an input word on each rising edge where in_valid and in_ready are both high. Presents the head word on out_data and asserts out_valid while nonempty; removes it on a rising edge where out_valid and out_ready are both high. A newly accepted word becomes visible after that edge, giving a minimum accepted-transfer age of one cycle. in_ready is high when the FIFO has space, including when a dequeue on the same edge frees space. Reset clears pointers and occupancy; out_data is zero while empty.",
