      "name": "uart_tx",
      "behavior": "UART 8N1 transmitter with public integer parameter DIV, default 868. When load is high while idle, captures data on the rising edge, drives tx low for the start bit, then shifts the eight data bits least-significant bit first, followed by a high stop bit. Each bit lasts exactly DIV clock cycles; tx remains high while idle and ignores load while busy. Synchronous active-high reset returns the transmitter to idle with tx high. The FIFO holds its head word until ready is high; ready is high only while the transmitter is idle, so load and ready describe the transfer cycle exactly.",
